# E-Learning Platform Infrastructure

## Overview

An e-learning company is looking to take advantage of a Government programme that retrains graduates into IT. Their current platform can't reliably meet student needs, so they need a more robust, scalable solution for orchestrating their containerised applications.

This repository contains the infrastructure-as-code to build that platform on AWS.

## Goals

- Replace the existing platform with one that is robust and able to scale with student demand
- Orchestrate Docker containers using Amazon ECS
- Provision all infrastructure consistently and repeatably using Terraform

## Architecture

- **Container orchestration:** Amazon ECS
- **Container images:** All applications are already containerised, with images stored in Amazon ECR
- **Application:** An Nginx server, deployed and managed by ECS
- **Infrastructure as code:** Terraform
- **CI/CD:** Jenkins, using a Jenkinsfile to deploy the code to AWS

## Environments

The Terraform code supports four separate environments:

| Environment | Purpose |
|-------------|---------|
| DEV         | Development and experimentation |
| TEST        | Automated and QA testing |
| STAGING     | Pre-production validation |
| PROD        | Live, student-facing platform |

## Deployment

Deployments are handled by a Jenkins pipeline defined in the `Jenkinsfile`. The pipeline runs the Terraform code to build and update the infrastructure in the target AWS environment.

## Prerequisites

- An AWS account with appropriate permissions
- Terraform installed
- Access to the Jenkins server
- Container images available in ECR
